menu "OnePlus async reclaim optimization"

config OPLUS_MEM_OPT_SUITE
	bool "Enable OnePlus Memory Optimization Suite"
	default n
	help
	  This option enables the entire suite of OnePlus memory management
	  optimizations, including the asynchronous LRU reclaim daemon,
	  asynchronous slab reclaim daemon, and the Per-CPU pages drain
	  bypass optimization.

	  If unsure, say N.

config OPLUS_SHRINK_LRUVECD_OPT
	bool "Oplus Asynchronous LRU Reclaim Daemon"
	depends on MMU && PROC_FS && TRACEPOINTS
	depends on OPLUS_MEM_OPT_SUITE
	default n
	help
	  This option enables the Oplus asynchronous LRU reclaim daemon
	  (kshrink_lruvecd).

	  This feature creates a dedicated kernel thread that handles
	  reclaiming pages that were skipped during synchronous vmscan
	  passes due to lock contention (e.g., page locks, mapping locks).

	  If unsure, say N.

config OPLUS_SHRINK_SLABD_OPT
	bool "Oplus Asynchronous Slab Reclaim Daemon"
	depends on MMU && TRACEPOINTS
	depends on OPLUS_MEM_OPT_SUITE
	help
	  This option enables the Oplus asynchronous slab reclaim daemon
	  (kshrink_slabd).

	  This feature creates a dedicated kernel thread to perform slab
	  reclaim asynchronously when triggered by allocation paths.

	  If unsure, say N.

config OPLUS_PCPAGES_OPT
	bool "Oplus Per-CPU Pages Drain Bypass Optimization"
	depends on MMU && TRACEPOINTS
	depends on OPLUS_MEM_OPT_SUITE
	help
	  This option enables an Oplus optimization that bypasses the
	  "drain all pages" operation in certain memory allocation paths.

	  The "drain all pages" operation typically moves pages from
	  per-CPU page caches (PCPs) to global free lists. Bypassing this
	  can reduce overhead in specific scenarios, aiming for faster
	  allocation attempts.

	  If unsure, say N.

config OPLUS_MAPPED_PROTECT_OPT
	bool "Oplus Mapped Page Protection Optimization"
	depends on MMU && PROC_FS && TRACEPOINTS
	default n
	help
	  This option enables the Oplus optimization for protecting heavily
	  mapped (shared) pages from being aggressively reclaimed under
	  memory pressure.

	  It tracks the number of pages mapped by 20 or more page tables
	  and uses thresholds based on system RAM and these counts to
	  conditionally prevent these pages from being selected for reclaim.

	  If unsure, say N.

config OPLUS_KSWAPD_ALLOC_ADJUST_OPT
	bool "Oplus kswapd high-order alloc adjust optimization"
	depends on MMU && JUMP_LABEL && TRACEPOINTS
	default n
	help
	  This option enables an Oplus optimization that modifies the
	  GFP flags for high-order memory allocations (above PAGE_ALLOC_COSTLY_ORDER).

	  When enabled, it removes the __GFP_RECLAIM flag for these allocations,
	  preventing them from directly triggering kswapd or waiting for reclaim.
	  This aims to reduce overhead for large allocations.

	  If unsure, say N.

endmenu
